            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had a frozen banana that I used in this smoothie which eliminated the need for ice. I also do not keep cream of coconut on hand but I did have some fat free evaporated milk--I used that and a half teaspoon of coconut extract. Very tasty smoothie. I'm glad that it didn't call for additional sugar because it was plenty sweet on it's own. Has a \"tropical\" feel to it. I liked this smoothie a lot."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Yoly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I believe the calorie count on this is wrong. Two tbs of cream of coconut have 240 calories and this smoothie calls for a quarter cup. That’s twice as much in calories, making it 480 calories for the cream of coconut alone! Needless to say I only used 2 tbs of the cream of coconut. All my fruit for the exception of the kiwi were frozen, eliminating the need for ice. I added 1/2 cup of almond milk because it was so thick. Though tasty, I don’t think I will make it again because of the high calorie count.",
            "datePublished": "2024-08-19T21:32:14.630Z"
          },
